WEBVTT

00:00:24.830 --> 00:00:26.040
How is it, Elia?

00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:27.620
It's almost ready.

00:00:27.620 --> 00:00:31.410
I will wake Mr. Ryoma then.

00:00:31.410 --> 00:00:32.790
Yes, please do!

00:00:32.790 --> 00:00:34.580
Of course, my lady.

00:00:35.620 --> 00:00:39.790
Huh? Did the lady wake up early to cook?

00:00:39.790 --> 00:00:46.450
Y-Yes... Though Mother and
the others helped, too, but, um...

00:00:46.450 --> 00:00:49.700
She says she wants to ask you a favor, Ryoma.

00:00:49.700 --> 00:00:52.580
So, um... Mr. Ryoma...

00:00:52.580 --> 00:00:55.120
Please teach me how to play with magic!

00:00:55.120 --> 00:00:56.370
Huh?

00:00:56.370 --> 00:00:58.000
Oh, of course!

00:00:59.790 --> 00:01:01.580
Like we promised.

00:01:01.580 --> 00:01:03.250
Congratulations, Elia.

00:01:03.250 --> 00:01:04.410
Yes.

00:01:04.410 --> 00:01:08.080
Is that what this breakfast was for?

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:09.330
Y-Yes...

00:01:09.330 --> 00:01:12.370
I'm grateful. Thank you for the food.

00:01:13.660 --> 00:01:15.290
How is it?

00:01:15.290 --> 00:01:16.330
It's delicious!

00:01:16.330 --> 00:01:17.950
I'm relieved!

00:01:17.950 --> 00:01:20.080
It really is good.

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:24.290
Come on, is it even possible
to fail with ham and eggs?

00:01:26.450 --> 00:01:27.700
Oops...

00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:34.500
Mr. Ryoma, would you like
to learn something, too?

00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:37.330
Are you sure? Well...

00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:39.700
In that case, I don't know
many attack magics, so...

00:01:39.700 --> 00:01:42.000
For that, the best teacher would be...

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:45.500
Me. You can count on me, Ryoma.

00:01:45.500 --> 00:01:48.250
Thank you, Mr. Camil.

00:03:18.950 --> 00:03:23.950
"Episode 5"
"The Lady's Training Session, with the Slimes"

00:03:29.290 --> 00:03:32.950
I'm ready, please teach me
how to play with magic!

00:03:32.950 --> 00:03:37.290
My lady, you're good at
ice and fire magic, right?

00:03:37.290 --> 00:03:38.410
Yes!

00:03:39.660 --> 00:03:41.790
Is that a problem?

00:03:41.790 --> 00:03:45.080
Those two are the hardest to play with.

00:03:45.080 --> 00:03:49.830
With ice magic, all you can do is
make ice sculptures, and with fire...

00:03:49.830 --> 00:03:51.080
Darkness.

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:54.080
Please watch.

00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:55.950
Little Fire Flower.

00:03:59.620 --> 00:04:01.540
Oh, how pretty.

00:04:04.080 --> 00:04:05.410
Would you like to try?

00:04:05.410 --> 00:04:07.290
It looked pretty, but...

00:04:07.290 --> 00:04:10.290
...the ending was a bit sad.

00:04:10.290 --> 00:04:12.370
It made me feel sentimental, for some reason.

00:04:12.370 --> 00:04:15.660
I guess sparkler fireworks
can have that effect...

00:04:15.660 --> 00:04:19.200
How about water magic?
You can use that as well, right?

00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:22.580
It's not my strongest, but I'll try!

00:04:22.580 --> 00:04:24.580
All right, please watch closely.

00:04:24.580 --> 00:04:25.700
Okay!

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:29.370
Bubbly Water!

00:04:32.660 --> 00:04:33.830
Breeze.

00:04:40.620 --> 00:04:43.750
Oh, how interesting.

00:04:43.750 --> 00:04:48.200
The key is to use this Bubbly Water magic
to add stickiness to the water.

00:04:48.200 --> 00:04:49.910
I'll try.

00:04:51.580 --> 00:04:53.540
Bubbly Water.

00:04:56.250 --> 00:04:57.370
Breeze.

00:05:05.080 --> 00:05:09.290
The ones you made haven't broken yet...

00:05:09.290 --> 00:05:15.330
Imagine the sticky solution from
the sticky slimes. A sticky, gummy feeling.

00:05:17.290 --> 00:05:19.500
A sticky feeling...

00:05:29.500 --> 00:05:32.950
Okay! Bubbly Water!

00:05:32.950 --> 00:05:34.080
Breeze.

00:05:38.870 --> 00:05:40.620
I did it!

00:05:40.620 --> 00:05:41.790
Great!

00:05:41.790 --> 00:05:43.080
Wow!

00:05:43.080 --> 00:05:46.250
If you practice, you can
do something like this, too.

00:05:46.250 --> 00:05:48.160
Bubbly Water.

00:05:48.160 --> 00:05:49.450
Breeze.

00:05:51.200 --> 00:05:52.870
So big...!

00:05:52.870 --> 00:05:54.120
--Here.
--Huh?!

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:55.540
You, too, my lady!

00:05:57.410 --> 00:05:59.910
Interesting, this one lasts quite long.

00:05:59.910 --> 00:06:04.330
Putting in some extra magic power
makes them stickier and harder to break.

00:06:04.330 --> 00:06:06.700
I see, I see.

00:06:06.700 --> 00:06:10.950
This is starting to look like a slime.

00:06:10.950 --> 00:06:14.660
Good, she seems to be enjoying this.

00:06:14.660 --> 00:06:15.750
There!

00:06:15.750 --> 00:06:19.290
I know, let's mix it up a bit.

00:06:19.290 --> 00:06:20.790
Mix it up?

00:06:20.790 --> 00:06:22.910
Yes. Water.

00:06:25.910 --> 00:06:27.000
Wave.

00:06:38.370 --> 00:06:42.290
You can change the shape
of the water, like this.

00:06:42.290 --> 00:06:44.120
A big fish...!

00:06:46.040 --> 00:06:47.870
Swimming in the sky...!

00:06:47.870 --> 00:06:49.200
Wonderful...

00:06:49.200 --> 00:06:50.580
Impressive.

00:06:50.580 --> 00:06:53.290
I like how you think.

00:06:55.450 --> 00:06:57.700
What do you think, my lady?

00:06:57.700 --> 00:07:00.500
Now I think I can enjoy playing with magic!

00:07:00.500 --> 00:07:02.200
Thank you so much!

00:07:04.870 --> 00:07:07.660
I'm glad I could help.

00:07:08.700 --> 00:07:10.580
Come on, you can do it!

00:07:10.580 --> 00:07:11.870
Y-Yes!

00:07:13.500 --> 00:07:15.620
Shall we do our own work, too, now?

00:07:15.620 --> 00:07:17.580
Yes, please!

00:07:17.580 --> 00:07:20.410
First, here's a fire attack magic.

00:07:23.500 --> 00:07:25.330
Fire Arrow.

00:07:29.580 --> 00:07:35.120
This is the fire attack magic
that's most usable and popular.

00:07:35.120 --> 00:07:36.500
I'll try it out!

00:07:38.200 --> 00:07:40.200
Imagine an arrow...

00:07:40.200 --> 00:07:41.950
Fire Arrow!

00:07:46.750 --> 00:07:50.410
Great, you got it in one try.

00:07:50.410 --> 00:07:51.870
Next is...

00:07:53.700 --> 00:07:56.160
Water Shot!

00:07:56.160 --> 00:07:57.870
After that, Mr. Camil taught me

00:07:57.870 --> 00:08:01.620
Water Shot, Wind Hammer, Rock Bullet,

00:08:01.620 --> 00:08:03.830
Stun Arrow, Ice Arrow...

00:08:03.830 --> 00:08:06.370
And some defensive magic, like Fire Wall,

00:08:06.370 --> 00:08:12.000
Water Wall, Wind Shield, and Ice Shield.

00:08:13.330 --> 00:08:15.870
Mr. Camil, what's next?

00:08:15.870 --> 00:08:21.160
Well, you've learned all that
I wanted to teach you today, so...

00:08:21.160 --> 00:08:22.910
What to do now...

00:08:22.910 --> 00:08:26.580
In that case, I shall teach you
some space magic.

00:08:26.580 --> 00:08:27.660
Are you sure?!

00:08:27.660 --> 00:08:28.950
Yes, of course.

00:08:28.950 --> 00:08:30.870
You're in luck, Ryoma.

00:08:30.870 --> 00:08:32.660
Thank you!

00:08:33.660 --> 00:08:39.200
Mr. Ryoma, have you learned
any space magic other than Item Box?

00:08:39.200 --> 00:08:40.910
I can use Teleport.

00:08:40.910 --> 00:08:43.330
Can you show us?

00:08:43.330 --> 00:08:44.870
Of course.

00:08:44.870 --> 00:08:46.200
Teleport!

00:08:51.580 --> 00:08:52.790
Like that.

00:08:52.790 --> 00:08:54.500
Wonderful.

00:08:55.370 --> 00:09:01.580
You should be ready to learn intermediate
space magic, like Dimension Home and Warp.

00:09:01.580 --> 00:09:02.790
Really?!

00:09:02.790 --> 00:09:05.000
Yes, truly.

00:09:05.000 --> 00:09:08.450
All space magics are basically the same.

00:09:08.450 --> 00:09:14.620
For example, for Warp, if you can get
a solid mental image of your destination,

00:09:14.620 --> 00:09:18.370
you should be able to travel as far as you want,
as long as you have the magic energy.

00:09:18.370 --> 00:09:19.790
Mental image...

00:09:24.080 --> 00:09:25.950
I feel like I can do it. I will try.

00:09:25.950 --> 00:09:27.540
Please.

00:09:27.540 --> 00:09:29.750
Here I go. Warp.

00:09:35.000 --> 00:09:37.250
Wow, I really did it!

00:09:37.250 --> 00:09:38.250
Whoa!

00:09:39.160 --> 00:09:44.950
Congratulations, you have successfully
cast Warp, the intermediate space magic.

00:09:44.950 --> 00:09:47.660
Thank you, Mr. Sebas!

00:09:47.660 --> 00:09:52.790
Moving on, let us now practice Dimension Home.

00:09:52.790 --> 00:09:57.500
Dimension Home is a magic that's
a straight improvement of Item Box.

00:09:57.500 --> 00:10:01.910
It creates a huge space
that can hold much more stuff,

00:10:01.910 --> 00:10:06.040
and unlike Item Box, there's air inside,

00:10:06.040 --> 00:10:08.620
which means living things can be kept in it.

00:10:08.620 --> 00:10:13.080
If I can master this, it would
help me carry my slimes around.

00:10:31.250 --> 00:10:32.910
Dimension Home.

00:10:38.790 --> 00:10:41.660
Did I do it? Mr. Sebas!

00:10:45.330 --> 00:10:49.910
Congratulations. You have
successfully cast Dimension Home.

00:10:49.910 --> 00:10:53.450
Now I can carry my slimes around! Thank you!

00:10:53.450 --> 00:10:56.250
It was all thanks to your hard work, Mr. Ryoma.

00:10:56.250 --> 00:10:58.450
I am happy for you, too.

00:10:58.450 --> 00:11:04.660
Let us return to the lady.
It is getting dark soon.

00:11:04.660 --> 00:11:07.500
What?! Already?!

00:11:07.500 --> 00:11:12.040
You were so focused, you lost track of time.

00:11:12.040 --> 00:11:13.120
Shall we?

00:11:13.120 --> 00:11:14.790
Yes.

00:11:14.790 --> 00:11:16.040
Warp.

00:11:18.040 --> 00:11:20.410
No, Worgan and I are <i>not </i>dating!

00:11:22.750 --> 00:11:26.620
This softness, it makes me
never want to get back up...

00:11:27.500 --> 00:11:32.750
The next day, we went to
the abandoned North Gimul Mine.

00:11:32.750 --> 00:11:37.200
The goal was to train the lady
in monster combat skills.

00:11:37.200 --> 00:11:40.620
The duty of every noble is to
protect their land and its citizens.

00:11:40.620 --> 00:11:43.160
This means that sometimes,
when monsters or bandits appear,

00:11:43.160 --> 00:11:45.950
we must join the fight against them.

00:11:45.950 --> 00:11:47.450
The lady, too?

00:11:47.450 --> 00:11:52.040
Of course. That is the duty of
those born into the ducal family.

00:11:52.040 --> 00:11:57.700
Combat training, various magic,
etiquette, civics, and economics...

00:11:57.700 --> 00:12:01.290
There is so much more to learn.

00:12:01.290 --> 00:12:03.250
I see.

00:12:03.250 --> 00:12:06.950
Yes. That's why, after this trip,
I'm going to the royal capital

00:12:06.950 --> 00:12:09.500
to attend the school there.

00:12:09.500 --> 00:12:10.910
I see...

00:12:12.790 --> 00:12:17.160
Ah. So she's going to the capital soon...

00:12:20.160 --> 00:12:21.910
Dimension Home.

00:12:27.950 --> 00:12:31.450
So. M'lady, Ryoma, are you ready?

00:12:31.450 --> 00:12:32.450
Y-Yes!

00:12:32.450 --> 00:12:33.290
Yes!

00:12:33.290 --> 00:12:34.500
Here we go!

00:12:39.330 --> 00:12:41.620
Be careful, everyone!

00:12:41.620 --> 00:12:44.000
Good luck, Elia!

00:12:44.000 --> 00:12:46.620
We await your return.

00:12:46.620 --> 00:12:49.910
Duke Reinhart's group went to
a different part of the mines

00:12:49.910 --> 00:12:54.950
to investigate how infested
with monsters the mine shafts are.

00:12:55.700 --> 00:12:57.950
Depending on the type and number of monsters,

00:12:57.950 --> 00:13:02.790
they will determine whether or not to
issue a quest at the Adventurer's Guild.

00:13:02.790 --> 00:13:07.450
That's right. Duke Reinhart,
the madam, and Sir Reinbach

00:13:07.450 --> 00:13:11.200
are all really strong and
don't actually need us guards.

00:13:11.200 --> 00:13:16.290
The types of monsters to hang out in
mines like these are no match for them.

00:13:16.290 --> 00:13:18.750
So there's no need to worry about them.

00:13:18.750 --> 00:13:21.160
You should just be worried about yourselves.

00:13:21.160 --> 00:13:23.790
Right... M'lady, young sir,

00:13:23.790 --> 00:13:27.580
this doesn't apply here since these mines
were a place where people worked,

00:13:27.580 --> 00:13:31.450
but if this were a labyrinth,
you may encounter traps.

00:13:31.450 --> 00:13:35.500
It's the job of scouts like me
to find those things.

00:13:35.500 --> 00:13:39.370
Please do try to make sure
you don't get ahead of us.

00:13:39.370 --> 00:13:40.580
I understand!

00:13:40.580 --> 00:13:41.870
Understood.

00:13:48.790 --> 00:13:51.160
A praying mantis... but huge?

00:13:51.160 --> 00:13:52.950
That's a cave mantis.

00:13:52.950 --> 00:13:56.080
Ugh, what a bother.

00:13:56.080 --> 00:13:58.660
A bother... Are they dangerous?

00:13:58.660 --> 00:14:02.700
They aren't. But they breed quickly,

00:14:02.700 --> 00:14:06.250
so if you see one,
you should expect at least 30.

00:14:06.250 --> 00:14:08.000
Wow...

00:14:08.000 --> 00:14:10.000
You're up, m'lady!

00:14:10.000 --> 00:14:12.250
Y-Yes!

00:14:12.250 --> 00:14:15.870
Their arm attacks can be
somewhat fast, so watch out for that.

00:14:15.870 --> 00:14:20.660
No fire magic. In caves,
there's no place for the smoke to go.

00:14:20.660 --> 00:14:22.200
I understand!

00:14:32.000 --> 00:14:33.620
Ice Arrow!

00:14:39.410 --> 00:14:40.910
Ice Arrow!

00:14:48.410 --> 00:14:49.910
I did it!

00:14:49.910 --> 00:14:52.750
The speed of your magic activation is fine,

00:14:52.750 --> 00:14:56.040
but please try to be more accurate next time.

00:14:56.040 --> 00:14:58.250
Yes, I understand.

00:15:00.080 --> 00:15:02.290
That was a success!

00:15:02.290 --> 00:15:03.790
Yes!

00:15:06.540 --> 00:15:13.370
Since the lady just went,
I was going to say Ryoma's up next, but...

00:15:13.370 --> 00:15:15.700
...is four at once too much for a start?

00:15:15.700 --> 00:15:16.700
I'll give it a try.

00:15:16.700 --> 00:15:18.620
Good luck!

00:15:18.620 --> 00:15:20.330
Don't push yourself too much.

00:15:20.330 --> 00:15:21.450
Right.

00:15:23.750 --> 00:15:25.200
Physical Hardening...

00:15:56.200 --> 00:15:59.450
I guess his close quarters
fighting is fine, too.

00:16:01.160 --> 00:16:04.160
M'lady, remember,
insect-type monsters are resilient.

00:16:04.160 --> 00:16:07.540
Don't let your guard down until
you've taken off or crushed their heads.

00:16:07.540 --> 00:16:08.750
Got it!

00:16:10.750 --> 00:16:13.790
We continued to search through the mineshaft.

00:16:13.790 --> 00:16:17.750
The lady and I defeated many cave mantises.

00:16:19.160 --> 00:16:23.040
That should be good. We should head back now.

00:16:28.620 --> 00:16:31.700
That's... a metal slime!

00:16:34.200 --> 00:16:36.700
There's a metal slime?!

00:16:36.700 --> 00:16:38.620
I'll catch it!

00:16:41.870 --> 00:16:43.790
Ice Shield.

00:16:45.120 --> 00:16:46.700
Ice Shield.

00:16:48.870 --> 00:16:51.250
There's nowhere left to run.

00:16:54.540 --> 00:16:56.120
I caught it.

00:16:56.120 --> 00:16:58.000
Congratulations.

00:16:59.040 --> 00:17:01.000
You should enter a Taming Contract right away...

00:17:01.000 --> 00:17:02.910
Here you are, Mr. Ryoma.

00:17:02.910 --> 00:17:03.910
Huh?

00:17:06.950 --> 00:17:10.160
This is to thank you for
teaching me how to play with magic.

00:17:10.160 --> 00:17:11.580
Are you sure?

00:17:11.580 --> 00:17:13.200
Of course.

00:17:13.200 --> 00:17:16.410
Thank you! I'm so happy!

00:17:18.540 --> 00:17:21.410
You should enter a Taming Contract right away.

00:17:21.410 --> 00:17:23.540
Oh, yes, right.

00:17:29.120 --> 00:17:33.500
I see, it seems like this is
now a nest of cave mantises.

00:17:33.500 --> 00:17:37.040
Our mineshaft had cave bats.

00:17:37.040 --> 00:17:42.200
I suppose it would be best to issue
a quest through the Adventurer's Guild.

00:17:42.200 --> 00:17:43.580
I agree.

00:17:53.160 --> 00:17:57.410
You're really heavy. Do you eat metal?

00:17:57.410 --> 00:17:58.750
Metal...?

00:18:00.080 --> 00:18:04.200
The red soil here, that's the color
of oxidized iron, right...?

00:18:04.200 --> 00:18:08.410
The iron ore might be depleted,
but maybe there's still some iron left here...?

00:18:09.790 --> 00:18:10.910
Right.

00:18:13.910 --> 00:18:20.160
Use alchemy to separate
the iron from the soil...

00:18:20.160 --> 00:18:21.370
Separation.

00:18:22.250 --> 00:18:25.410
Then separate out the oxygen
which is making the rust...

00:18:25.410 --> 00:18:26.700
Combination!

00:18:26.700 --> 00:18:27.950
Consolidate...

00:18:31.660 --> 00:18:32.750
Success!

00:18:32.750 --> 00:18:35.120
Wh-What was that magic?!

00:18:35.120 --> 00:18:36.540
Wonderful...

00:18:36.540 --> 00:18:37.910
Oh...

00:18:37.910 --> 00:18:40.200
Is that the alchemy you mentioned?

00:18:40.200 --> 00:18:46.290
Y-Yes. I thought maybe I could
get iron out of the red soil.

00:18:47.120 --> 00:18:50.660
That's the first time I've seen real,
non-fraudulent alchemy.

00:18:50.660 --> 00:18:52.660
So it really does exist...

00:18:52.660 --> 00:18:55.000
I am surprised.

00:18:55.000 --> 00:19:00.290
This iron, it's beautiful. Like a mirror.

00:19:00.290 --> 00:19:02.080
Oh, I remember.

00:19:02.080 --> 00:19:06.580
I forgot about this, but there was someone
I wanted to introduce Ryoma to.

00:19:06.580 --> 00:19:08.000
Introduce...?

00:19:11.040 --> 00:19:17.000
Sir Reinbach took me to a shop
named "Morgan Trading Company."

00:19:20.660 --> 00:19:21.950
Here it is.

00:19:24.830 --> 00:19:27.450
I see, this is...

00:19:28.330 --> 00:19:34.500
Mr. Ryoma Takebayashi, a real alchemist...!

00:19:34.500 --> 00:19:37.000
Oh, please, there's no need for that.

00:19:40.250 --> 00:19:46.080
And all of these great items,
like the waterproof cloth...

00:19:46.080 --> 00:19:51.000
I understand, Sir Reinbach. I, Serge Morgan
of the Morgan Trading Company,

00:19:51.000 --> 00:19:55.910
will take on the responsibility
of selling these fine goods.

00:19:55.910 --> 00:20:00.250
Yes. If done right, they should
raise astounding profits.

00:20:00.250 --> 00:20:02.000
Um...

00:20:02.000 --> 00:20:05.450
I would like to keep it a secret
that I'm the one making them.

00:20:05.450 --> 00:20:07.410
Why is that?

00:20:07.410 --> 00:20:11.040
If word gets out that Ryoma is a real alchemist,

00:20:11.040 --> 00:20:14.250
some might begin to suspect fraud.

00:20:14.250 --> 00:20:17.330
Also, he's only 11 years old...

00:20:18.580 --> 00:20:25.000
There is the risk that some would
use nefarious means to take him in.

00:20:25.000 --> 00:20:28.830
Also, I'd like to make sure
all of the profits go to Ryoma.

00:20:28.830 --> 00:20:32.160
What?! That's too generous...

00:20:32.160 --> 00:20:36.250
You invented it, and you made it.
It's only natural.

00:20:36.250 --> 00:20:38.500
Don't be modest.

00:20:38.500 --> 00:20:41.370
Yes! It belongs to you!

00:20:43.370 --> 00:20:47.500
We don't need the money.

00:20:47.500 --> 00:20:51.450
Everyone... Thank you...

00:20:51.450 --> 00:20:56.450
Of course. Serge is a trustworthy merchant.
There is nothing to worry about.

00:20:56.450 --> 00:20:59.910
Right. Thank you, Mr. Serge.

00:20:59.910 --> 00:21:06.160
The pleasure is mine. Please come visit again.

00:21:06.160 --> 00:21:08.660
These are all such nice people.

00:21:08.660 --> 00:21:11.910
They welcome me, they worry about me,

00:21:11.910 --> 00:21:14.790
and they're truly looking out for me.

00:21:15.750 --> 00:21:18.500
I'm truly, truly happy...

00:21:22.160 --> 00:21:26.540
And so, after the ducal family's
thorough investigation,

00:21:26.540 --> 00:21:31.250
all of those who were embezzling the budget
for the pit toilets were arrested.

00:21:31.250 --> 00:21:33.040
Meow wonderful!

00:21:33.040 --> 00:21:35.120
Not bad, Duke.

00:21:35.120 --> 00:21:39.660
Yeah. So, no need to worry about that anymore.

00:21:40.620 --> 00:21:46.370
The next job I have for you is a monster hunt
in the abandoned mine shafts.

00:21:46.370 --> 00:21:47.790
The mines?

00:21:47.790 --> 00:21:49.830
You mean the North Gimul Mines?

00:21:49.830 --> 00:21:50.910
Yes.

00:21:50.910 --> 00:21:53.330
Any tough monsters?

00:21:53.330 --> 00:21:57.160
The monsters are all small,
but who knows what could be down there.

00:21:57.160 --> 00:21:59.830
Work together as a team to get this done.

00:21:59.830 --> 00:22:01.580
This begins tomorrow morning!

00:22:01.580 --> 00:22:02.410
Right!

00:22:02.410 --> 00:22:03.250
Understood.

00:22:03.250 --> 00:22:05.250
Gotcha!

00:22:05.250 --> 00:22:10.160
And so I took on a new mission.

00:22:10.160 --> 00:22:15.040
I'll stay focused and sharp
so that I don't burden the others.
